{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P34689","secondaryAccessions":["Q22873","Q7KQH5","Q9TXH4"],"uniProtkbId":"GLH1_CAEEL","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"1994-02-01","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2004-08-16","entryVersion":189,"sequenceVersion":3},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Caenorhabditis elegans","taxonId":6239,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Ecdysozoa","Nematoda","Chromadorea","Rhabditida","Rhabditina","Rhabditomorpha","Rhabditoidea","Rhabditidae","Peloderinae","Caenorhabditis"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"ATP-dependent RNA helicase glh-1"},"ecNumbers":[{"value":"3.6.4.13"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Germline helicase 1"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"WormBase","id":"T21G5.3"}],"value":"glh-1"},"orfNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"WormBase","id":"T21G5.3"}],"value":"T21G5.3"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18234720"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21402787"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24746798"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"27650246"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"28533440"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"8415696"}],"value":"Probable ATP-binding RNA helicase (PubMed:8415696). May act redundantly with the P-granule component glh-4 to regulate the formation of the granular structure of P-granules in embryos (PubMed:21402787, PubMed:24746798). Plays a role in positively regulating the localization of pgl-1 to P-granules (PubMed:18234720). May play a role in transgenerational epigenetic inheritance (PubMed:28533440). May protect somatic cells from excessive apoptosis during normal development (PubMed:27650246)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"ATP + H2O = ADP + phosphate + H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:13065"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:43474"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:456216"}],"ecNumber":"3.6.4.13"}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12435362"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17699606"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22342905"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"17699606"}],"value":"Interacts with csn-5; this may prevent glh-1 degradation induced by kgb-1 (PubMed:12435362, PubMed:17699606). Interacts with zyx-1 (PubMed:12435362). Interacts (via the N-terminal region containing the four CCHC zinc fingers) with pan-1 (PubMed:22342905). Interacts with kgb-1; this may promote glh-1 degradation by the proteasome (PubMed:17699606)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P34689","intActId":"EBI-1571791"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P91001","geneName":"csn-5","intActId":"EBI-313007"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P34689","intActId":"EBI-1571791"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O01836","geneName":"glh-3","intActId":"EBI-1571750"},"numberOfExperiments":2,"organismDiffer":false}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17699606"}],"value":"Perinuclear localization in germ cells but disperses into particles in cellularized oocytes. Component of P granules"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17699606"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21402787"}],"value":"Cytoplasm","id":"SL-0086"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17699606"}],"value":"Cytoplasmic granule","id":"SL-0281"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17699606"}],"value":"Cytoplasm, perinuclear region","id":"SL-0198"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8415696"}],"value":"First expressed during the L3-L4 stages of larval development, coinciding with germline proliferation"}],"commentType":"DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17699606"}],"value":"Phosphorylated by kgb-1 (in vitro); this may be responsible for its degradation by the proteasome"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21402787"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24746798"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"27650246"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28533440"}],"value":"Mortal germline (Mrt) phenotype in which there is a progressive decline in fertility with each generation at 25 degrees Celsius (PubMed:28533440). RNAi-mediated knockdown in a glh-4 mutant background results in smaller P-granules and irregular cytoplasmic localization of the P-granule component pgl-3 in embryos (PubMed:21402787). Quadruple RNAi-mediated knockdown with glh-4, pgl-1 and pgl-3 results in offspring that display 27-89% sterility, abnormal oocytes and do not have embryos in the uterus (PubMed:24746798). These sterile offspring still produce sperm (PubMed:24746798). Furthermore, these offspring may have compromised P-granule integrity as there is diffuse cytoplasmic localization of the P-granule component deps-1, which may cause germ cells to initiate somatic reprogramming (PubMed:24746798). RNAi-mediated knockdown in a double ced-1 and hpl-2 mutant background rescues the reduced somatic cell apoptotic cell defect in the ced-1 and hpl-2 double knockout (PubMed:27650246)"}],"commentType":"DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the DEAD box helicase family. DDX4/VASA subfamily"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":763,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"ATP-dependent RNA helicase glh-1","featureId":"PRO_0000055089"},{"type":"Repeat","location":{"start":{"value":24,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":33,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"1"},{"type":"Repeat","location":{"start":{"value":34,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":43,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"2"},{"type":"Repeat","location":{"start":{"value":44,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":53,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"3"},{"type":"Repeat","location":{"start":{"value":54,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":63,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"4"},{"type":"Repeat","location":{"start":{"value":64,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":73,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"5"},{"type":"Repeat","location":{"start":{"value":74,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":83,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"6"},{"type":"Repeat","location":{"start":{"value":84,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":93,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"7"},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":372,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":556,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helicase ATP-binding","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"PROSITE-ProRule","id":"PRU00541"}]},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":592,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":739,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helicase C-terminal","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"PROSITE-ProRule","id":"PRU00542"}]},{"type":"Zinc finger","location":{"start":{"value":158,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":175,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"CCHC-type 1","evidences":[{"evidenceC